      "description": "<figure><img width=\"879\" height=\"495\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_takeme2space_satellite.jpg?fit=879%2C495&amp;ssl=1\" class=\"attachment-rss-image-size size-rss-image-size wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_takeme2space_satellite.jpg?w=879&amp;ssl=1 879w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_takeme2space_satellite.jpg?resize=300%2C169&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_takeme2space_satellite.jpg?resize=768%2C432&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_takeme2space_satellite.jpg?resize=780%2C439&amp;ssl=1 780w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_takeme2space_satellite.jpg?resize=400%2C225&amp;ssl=1 400w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_takeme2space_satellite.jpg?resize=706%2C398&amp;ssl=1 706w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_takeme2space_satellite.jpg?fit=879%2C495&amp;ssl=1&amp;w=370 370w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 34.9rem) calc(100vw - 2rem), (max-width: 53rem) calc(8 * (100vw / 12)), (min-width: 53rem) calc(6 * (100vw / 12)), 100vw\" /></figure>\n<p>COLORADO SPRINGS – After announcing a $5 million seed round in January, Indian startup TakeMe2Space seeks to raise $55 million to establish a 50-kilowatt orbital data center. “What is key for us is to demonstrate that we can play the orbital data center game globally,” TakeMe2Space founder Ronak Kumar Samantray told SpaceNews. “There&#8217;s a lot [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://spacenews.com/indias-takeme2space-sets-sights-on-50-kilowatt-data-center/\">India&#8217;s TakeMe2Space sets sights on 50-kilowatt data center</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://spacenews.com\">SpaceNews</a>.</p>\n",
      "pub_date": "Thu, 16 Apr 2026 23:59:03 +0000",
      "source": "Space News",
      "data_coleta": "2026-04-18",
      "tentativas": 0,
      "status": "publicado",
