    {
      "title": "Volunteers Discover Rare Space Weather Events Using Their Ears",
      "link": "https://science.nasa.gov/get-involved/citizen-science/volunteers-discover-rare-space-weather-events-using-their-ears/",
      "description": "Scientists are working to understand exactly how these waves behave, and the team behind NASA’s Heliophysics Audified: Resonances in Plasmas (HARP) citizen science project approaches this in a unique way: they compare the Earth’s magnetic field to a giant harp in space.",
      "pub_date": "Fri, 17 Apr 2026 15:04:32 +0000",
      "source": "Nasa News",
      "data_coleta": "2026-04-18",
      "tentativas": 0,
      "status": "publicado",
      "lead": "A ciência cidadã acaba de ouvir o que os instrumentos tradicionais deixaram passar. Usando uma técnica inovadora de audificação de dados, voluntários do projeto HARP, da NASA, descobriram eventos raros de clima espacial na magnetosfera terrestre. Ao transformar ondas de plasma em som, a equipe validou novas formas de entender como o escudo magnético da Terra reage às tempestades solares.",
      "category": "Ciência",
      "data_publicacao": "2026-04-19 09:43"
    },
    {
      "title": "Countering missile threats ‘left of launch’",
      "link": "https://spacenews.com/countering-missile-threats-left-of-launch/",
      "description": "<figure><img width=\"879\" height=\"586\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_55211398279_747ed3286d_o.jpg?fit=879%2C586&amp;ssl=1\" class=\"attachment-rss-image-size size-rss-image-size wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_55211398279_747ed3286d_o.jpg?w=879&amp;ssl=1 879w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_55211398279_747ed3286d_o.jpg?resize=300%2C200&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_55211398279_747ed3286d_o.jpg?resize=768%2C512&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_55211398279_747ed3286d_o.jpg?resize=780%2C520&amp;ssl=1 780w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_55211398279_747ed3286d_o.jpg?resize=400%2C267&amp;ssl=1 400w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_55211398279_747ed3286d_o.jpg?resize=706%2C471&amp;ssl=1 706w, https://i0.wp.com/spacenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/rsz_55211398279_747ed3286d_o.jpg?fit=879%2C586&amp;ssl=1&amp;w=370 370w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 34.9rem) calc(100vw - 2rem), (max-width: 53rem) calc(8 * (100vw / 12)), (min-width: 53rem) calc(6 * (100vw / 12)), 100vw\" /></figure>\n<p>COLORADO SPRINGS – U.S. government agencies are working with industry to develop tools to disrupt missiles before they take flight, a timespan called ‘left of launch.’ “We&#8217;re looking at different aspects of the threat as it evolves,” Erich Hernandez-Baquero, Raytheon Intelligence and Space vice president of space intelligence, surveillance, reconnaissance, said at the Space Symposium. [&#8230;]</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://spacenews.com/countering-missile-threats-left-of-launch/\">Countering missile threats &#8216;left of launch&#8217;</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://spacenews.com\">SpaceNews</a>.</p>\n",
      "pub_date": "Thu, 16 Apr 2026 23:05:42 +0000",
      "source": "Space News",
      "data_coleta": "2026-04-18",
      "tentativas": 0,
      "status": "publicado",
      "lead": "A segurança global ganha uma nova camada de proatividade com o avanço das tecnologias 'left of launch'. Especialistas e agências agora focam em sistemas integrados capazes de neutralizar mísseis hipersônicos e balísticos antes mesmo do lançamento. Uma inovação técnica que combina vigilância orbital persistente e precisão cirúrgica para redefinir as estratégias de contenção de ameaças.",
      "category": "Defesa Técnica",
      "data_publicacao": "2026-04-19 09:43"
    },
